Perfect! All tests now pass. The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to return the second element instead of `parts[0]` to return the first element. This caused it to return 'world' instead of 'hello' for the input 'hello world', and caused an IndexError for single-word inputs like 'solo'.

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now both tests pass successfully.
